    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "When should I use UMAP instead of PCA?",
        "answer": "Use UMAP for nonlinear neighborhood structure. Use PCA when linear components, direct loadings, or simpler reproducibility are more important."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which metric should I choose?",
        "answer": "Use Euclidean distance for scaled numeric data, cosine distance for document vectors, and Hamming or Jaccard distance for binary data."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can UMAP support clustering?",
        "answer": "Yes. Use more than two components, low minimum distance, and independent cluster validation because UMAP can alter density."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I transform new data?",
        "answer": "Yes. Reuse the fitted preprocessing steps and UMAP model, while checking that new data resembles the training distribution."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I make results reproducible?",
        "answer": "Set random_state, preserve preprocessing parameters, record package versions, and compare repeated runs when stability matters."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does this skill run UMAP automatically?",
        "answer": "No. It provides workflow guidance and examples for Claude, Codex, and Claude Code to adapt to your data."
